q &= (200\ \text{ft}^3/\text{s})(3600\ \text{s/h}) \\
&= 7.2 \times 10^5\ \text{ft}^3/\text{h} \\
t_d &= (3.6 \times 10^8\ \text{ft}^3)/(7.2 \times 10^5\ \text{ft}^3/\text{h}) \\
&= 500\ \text{h}
\end{aligned}
\]
\[
k = 0.23\ \text{h}^{-1}
\]

Substituting the values of $\dot{m}$, $q$, $t_d$, and $k$ into the equation yields
\[
\begin{aligned}
C_{\text{eq}} &= \frac{\dot{m}}{q(1 + kt_d)} \\
&= \frac{5.45 \times 10^{10}\ \frac{\text{pCi}}{\text{h}}}{\left( 7.2 \times 10^5\ \frac{\text{ft}^3}{\text{h}} \right) \left[ 1 + \left( 0.23\ \frac{1}{\text{h}} \right)(500\ \text{h}) \right]} \\
